cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use HeartShift, cite this software metadata and cite each underlying
  dataset separately under its own licence and citation requirements.
title: "HeartShift: An Auditable Benchmark for Hospital and Measurement-Policy Shift"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Huseyinli
    given-names: Abdulla
abstract: >-
  HeartShift is research software for auditable hospital-shift and
  structured missingness-policy experiments in historical clinical tabular
  datasets. It separates source-only model selection, zero-shot domain
  generalization, unlabelled-target adaptation, consumed-outcome research, and
  non-scientific pipeline smoke tests. It is not a medical device and does not
  establish clinical validity or prospective cardiovascular risk.
repository-code: "https://github.com/abdullahuseyinli-dot/heart-disease-risk-model-benchmark"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - clinical-tabular-data
  - domain-generalization
  - hospital-shift
  - missing-data
  - reproducible-research
